 {
  "id": "F2",
  "title": "Local gate work can keep running after its execution is forgotten",
  "file": "src/gates/executor.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "If writing a check's result fails (for example the land queue's log append or an event-store write), the gate stage reports an error, but the remaining gate checks keep running in the background. They keep using the shared gate slot and CPU, and a retry can end up waiting behind them.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "cd $TMPDIR/adj && bun f2.ts  (runs executeGate with checks [a: true, b: 'sleep 2; touch marker'] and an onResult hook that throws; waits 4s, then checks for the marker)",
    "output": "rejected: log write failed t= 1793363378549\nsecond check ran after rejection: true"
   },
   "evidence": "At base, run.ts runAll called the hook inline inside the loop (`const r = await runOne(c, cwd, signal); checks.push(r); onResult?.(r, \"check\");`). A throwing hook therefore rejected runLocalGates itself: the loop stopped, the slot was released and no later check started. At head the local executor pushes results into a queue, and executeGate (executor.ts:160-172) forwards them in a separate task: `const events = (async () => { for await (const event of execution.events) if (event.type === \"check\") hooks.onResult?.(...) })(); const [result] = await Promise.all([execution.result, events]); return result; } finally { onSettled(); signal.removeEventListener(\"abort\", abort); await cancellation; }`. When the forwarder rejects, there is no catch that cancels, so runLocalGates keeps going, as the repro confirms. runGateExecution then clears the stored handle because onSettled ran. The reviewer's second path, a discarded handle that is still live in this process, is hard to reach at head, because onSettled fires in `finally` once the execution is attached and the handle is cleared. Path (1) carries the verdict."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A landing log write fails while checks are running, or the engine replaces a stored execution belonging to another purpose or commit. The original check continues after its handle is forgotten, consuming a gate slot and running alongside replacement work.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate-486.LLvzcF/probe.ts\"",
    "output": "{\"claim\":\"F2-hook\",\"rejection\":\"log write failed\",\"handleCleared\":true,\"replacementPassed\":true,\"originalPidAlive\":true,\"occupiedSlots\":1}\n{\"claim\":\"F2-hook-cleanup\",\"originalPidAlive\":false,\"occupiedSlots\":0}\n{\"claim\":\"F2-discard\",\"replacementPassed\":true,\"handleCleared\":true,\"originalPidAlive\":true,\"occupiedSlots\":1}\n{\"claim\":\"F2-discard-cleanup\",\"originalPidAlive\":false,\"occupiedSlots\":0}\nall owned executions settled"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe used localExecutor and runGateExecution with real shell children, recording each child's own PID. A throwing onResult hook rejected the wrapper, cleared persisted gateExecution, and allowed replacement work to finish while the original child remained alive. A separate live execution with a mismatched stored purpose/SHA likewise survived replacement. Explicit cancellation and awaiting each original result stopped the children and released their slots. At head, `await Promise.all([execution.result, events])` rejects when event forwarding throws, but finally only invokes onSettled, removes the abort listener, and awaits `cancellation`, which remains undefined without an abort. gate-execution.ts:59-64 then clears the handle. Its lines 29-32 also discard mismatched handles without cancellation. At base, hooks ran synchronously inside the gate loop; a throwing hook unwound that loop and released its slot before subsequent checks started. The response adds cancellation on errors, awaits execution.result before onSettled, tracks live executions, and cancels/awaits a mismatched live handle before clearing it."
  }
 }
